POST /auth_keys HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1
Connection: close
Authorization: Basic bWFudWFsLW5hbWU6bWFudWFsLXBhc3N3b3Jk

# username: manual-name
# password: manual-password
# Answers 201 with a Location: /auth_keys/{id} header naming the new key's URI
# by its id, and the key itself in the body. The id is never the key: an auth
# key is a bearer token and stays out of URLs. Send the key as
# Authorization: Bearer <auth_key> from then on, and DELETE /auth_keys with that
# header to revoke it.
